Cell["\<\
ProductLog[z] is a function that gives the principal solution for to  w in \
z=we^w, and  ProductLog[k,z] is the kth solution. The principal solution, \
which is when there is no order in the input, is for k=0. Bottom line is, \
there are indeed two roots, let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s evaluate them numerically\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.972968952399102*^9, 3.9729690052884307`*^9}, {
  3.972969065620676*^9, 3.9729690929990664`*^9}, {3.972969178494813*^9, 
